Apparently this actually works in the exported build:

```gdscript
	var level_file_list := ResourceLoader.list_directory("res://levels")
	for level_file_name in level_file_list:
		var extension := level_file_name.get_extension()
		# For editor builds
		if (extension == "tscn"):
			all_levels.append(level_file_name.get_basename())
```

I just didn't have the "res://" on the directory, but this kind of goes to show the importance of consistency between editor and exported builds.  It's much harder to debug the exported builds, so when things aren't behaving the same, it's very time consuming to fix.

Also, you can strip the ".import" and ".remap" off of the directory list.
